.SH NAME
_printf \- formatted output to stdout

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include "main.h"
.PP
.B int _printf(const char *\fIformat\fR, ...);

.SH DESCRIPTION
_printf writes formatted output to the standard output stream.
The format string contains ordinary characters, written unchanged, and conversion specifiers that fetch and format arguments.

.SS Conversion Specifiers
.TP
.B %c
Prints a single character.
.TP
.B %s
Prints a string. If NULL is passed, prints (null).
.TP
.B %d
Prints a decimal integer.
.TP
.B %i
Prints an integer (same as %d).
.TP
.B %%
Prints a literal percent sign.

.SH RETURN VALUE
The number of characters printed, excluding the null byte.

.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
_printf("Hello %s\\n", "world");
.PP
Output: Hello world
.PP
_printf("Char: %c\\n", 'A');
.PP
Output: Char: A
.PP
_printf("Number: %d\\n", 42);
.PP
Output: Number: 42

